# Lecture 05H

## Epistasis

## Chapter 5

## Dr. Neil Voss

## Sept 29, 2026

=== layout: one-panel

# Learning objectives

@body

- Distinguish epistasis from dominance
- Trace how pathway blocks alter phenotypes
- Group genotypes to predict phenotype ratios
- Compare F2 and testcross outcomes

@notes

Use the flower, squash, and Labrador examples to explain phenotype grouping. The aim is to reconstruct ratios from the model, not memorize a catalog.

