=== layout: one-panel

# One locus can mask another

@body

- Bateson and Punnett: white parents &rarr; purple F1
- F2: [9 purple : 7 white]{color=purple}
- A recessive homozygote at either locus masks the other locus
- Both gene products are required
- This is [gene-gene interaction]{color=red}

=== layout: one-panel

# Use C and P for the two loci

@body

- C and P: functional alleles
- c and p: nonfunctional alleles
- cc: white, regardless of the P genotype
- pp: white, regardless of the C genotype
- [Epistasis]{color=red}: masking between loci
- The word means "standing upon"

=== layout: one-panel

# Two-step anthocyanin model

@body

- C: precursor &rarr; intermediate
- P: intermediate &rarr; [purple anthocyanin]{color=purple}
- Both steps required for purple flowers
- cc or pp blocks pigment production
- Anthocyanin biochemistry: Dooner et al., 1991

=== layout: one-panel

