# White-cat cross: why answer d works

@left

| Offspring phenotype | Count / 16 |
| --- | --- |
| White | 12 |
| [Black]{color=red} | 3 |
| Gray | 1 |

@right

- Black: one locus recessive; the other has a dominant allele
- Under this labeling: [A\_bb]{color=red}
- [Answer d]{color=red}
- Gene names can be exchanged
- The ratio alone does not identify the biological locus

=== layout: section
# Test Cross

=== layout: one-panel
# Test Cross Ratio
@body

- In a normal dihybrid cross
  - P\: AABB x aabb
  - F1\: AaBb x AaBb
  - F2\: 9\:3\:3\:1 phenotype ratio
- Double heterozygote Test cross
  - TC\: AaBb x aabb
  - What is the offspring phenotype ratio?

=== layout: one-panel
# Test Cross Ratio
@body

- In a normal dihybrid cross
  - P\: AABB x aabb
  - F1\: AaBb x AaBb
  - F2\: 9\:3\:3\:1 phenotype ratio
- Double heterozygote Test cross
  - TC\: AaBb x aabb
  - [It is 1\:1\:1\:1]{color=red}

